# Build outputs
build/
build_grpc/
*.o
*.obj
*.so
*.a
*.exe

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temp / scratch
tmp_*
/tmp/
*.log

# PowerPoint. The lock files are Office's; the backups are add_speaker_notes.ps1
# dumping the notes pages as they stood before a run, so a script can never take
# hand-written notes away without leaving a copy on disk.
~$*.pptx
presentation/notes_backup/
presentation/Intern_showcase_Dami_backup_*.pptx
data/_recover/

# Personal / local-only docs (not for the shared repo)
RESULTS.md
M9_REPORT.md
ARCHITECTURE.md

# Working notes and handoffs. These are written for me and for whoever picks the
# project up, not for a reader of the repo. They quote lab host names, internal
# addresses, dead ends and half-formed conclusions, and they go stale the moment
# a run is repeated. Untracked on 2026-08-26. They are still in the history of
# earlier commits; removing them from there is a separate job.
PROGRESS.md
SHORTTERM_CONTEXT.md
LONGTERM_CONTEXT.md
handoff.md
handoff_roce_2026-08-06.md
presentation/HANDOFF.md

# Raw measurement data. Hundreds of per-run CSVs, large, and only meaningful
# next to the notes that say how each was paced. The two exceptions below are
# tracked on purpose: every chart in presentation/figs is generated from them,
# so the figures have to be reproducible from a clone alone.
data/*.csv
data/nsight/*.csv
!data/deck_4arm_4mib.csv
!data/headline_runs.csv

# Copies of NI and third-party source pulled onto this laptop off the Spark for
# reference while working. Not ours to republish.
data/*.h
data/*.cc
data/*.rs
data/*.diff
data/RDMA_TRANSPORT.md

# Scratch capture from remote sessions: command output, host inventories,
# build logs. Carries machine names and absolute paths. A few of these were
# tracked before this rule existed and stay tracked; the rule is for new ones.
data/*.out
data/*.txt
data/*.log

# PROGRESS.md, SHORTTERM_CONTEXT.md and LONGTERM_CONTEXT.md were listed here,
# then removed on 2026-08-20 because four tracked files pointed readers at them
# (handoff.md, handoff_roce_2026-08-06.md, scripts/find_spark.sh and
# presentation/HANDOFF.md), which made them handoff artifacts nobody outside
# this laptop could read.
#
# On 2026-08-26 they went back to being untracked, along with the handoff files
# that cited them. The 2026-08-20 argument only held while the handoffs were
# public; now the whole set is local, so nothing tracked points at a file a
# reader cannot open. scripts/find_spark.sh is the one loose end.
#
# Note that untracking does not remove them from earlier commits.

